  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member who follows a `cat=prive` link from a message, I want the same actions as when I open that conversation from Messages, so that every entry point to a conversation behaves the same (LESSONS 7). This is the only topic/MP split the review found on the write paths (operator's watch item of 2026-11-15 on #775).\n\n### What the review found on the watch item\nTopic and MP share one path: the same `TopicReaderView`, `TopicReaderModel`, `MessageWriteModel`, `ReaderReplyFlow` and `ReaderEditFlow`; the composer reports one `CloseReason`. Reply, quote, edit, delete, flags and reload have no second implementation. The two differences: `showLatestPost` (`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderModel.swift:393-400`, justified by a missing capture for `cat=prive`), and this one.\n\n### Scenario\nFollow a link to a private conversation from a message. The pushed reader shows it without \"Répondre\", \"Citer\", \"Editer\" or \"Supprimer\"; the same conversation opened from Messages has all four.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:152-153`: `// A private conversation reached from a topic offers no reply: MP replies are LOT-128's (no composer in Messages).` then `composer: linked.model.isPrivateConversation ? nil : composer`.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Messages/MessagesRootView.swift:45-58`: the Messages reader does receive the composer (\"Répondre on a conversation (LOT-128)\"), so the comment's reason is gone.\n- `composer == nil` removes the reply button, `writes` and `model.quoting`.\n\n### Fix\nPass `composer` unconditionally and delete the stale comment. If the restriction is wanted, state the real reason and add a GAP row (operator's call).\n\n### Test (fails before the fix)\nExtract the choice into a pure static (as `ReaderSearchFlow.isOffered`) and assert a linked private conversation gets the composer; or a hosted test that the linked MP reader shows the reply button.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5. Refs #908.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
